## Phase 6: Maintenance & Monitoring

### 6.1 Application Performance Monitoring (APM)

**Recommended Stack:**

| Tool | Purpose | Cost |
|---|---|---|
| **Sentry** | Error tracking, exception alerts, performance tracing | Free tier available |
| **Grafana Cloud** | Metrics dashboards, LLM latency tracking | Free tier (10k metrics) |
| **Prometheus** | Time-series metrics from Flask | Open source |
| **Datadog** | Full-stack APM (if budget allows) | ~$15/host/month |

**Minimum viable setup — Sentry:**
```bash
pip install sentry-sdk[flask]
```

```python
# app.py — Add after imports
import sentry_sdk
from sentry_sdk.integrations.flask import FlaskIntegration

sentry_sdk.init(
    dsn=os.environ.get("SENTRY_DSN"),
    integrations=[FlaskIntegration()],
    traces_sample_rate=0.2,       # 20% of requests profiled
    profiles_sample_rate=0.1,
    environment=os.environ.get("FLASK_ENV", "production"),
)
```

### 6.2 Custom Metrics to Track

```python
# Add to _save_message() and chat route
# These feed into your admin dashboard and Grafana:

METRICS_TO_TRACK = {
    "llm_latency_ms":        "P50/P95/P99 of LLM response time",
    "intent_distribution":   "Breakdown of query types",
    "cache_hit_rate":        "Redis cache effectiveness",
    "emergency_trigger_rate":"% of queries triggering emergency",
    "vision_usage_rate":     "Image analysis request volume",
    "error_rate":            "5xx rates per endpoint",
    "dau_mau":               "Daily/Monthly Active Users",
    "session_length":        "Average messages per conversation",
    "satisfaction_score":    "Thumbs up / (thumbs up + thumbs down)",
}
```

### 6.3 Alerting Rules

Set up these alerts in PagerDuty / Opsgenie / SNS:

| Alert | Threshold | Severity |
|---|---|---|
| LLM error rate | >5% over 5 min | P1 — page on-call |
| Average response latency | >10s P95 | P2 — Slack alert |
| Emergency keyword triggers | >20 in 1hr | P1 — review for crisis pattern |
| Failed logins | >100 in 10min (same IP) | P1 — possible credential stuffing |
| DB connection pool exhausted | Any | P1 |
| Pinecone unavailable | >1 min | P2 |
| OpenRouter API quota approaching | 80% of limit | P2 |

### 6.4 Log Hygiene

**Current `flask.log` problem:** It logs `Query: 'i want to kill myself...'` — raw user PII and sensitive mental health content — to a plain text file on disk and to stdout (visible in Docker logs).

**Fix log format to redact PII:**
```python
import re

def redact_pii(text: str) -> str:
    text = re.sub(r'\b[\w.-]+@[\w.-]+\.\w+\b', '[EMAIL]', text)
    text = re.sub(r'\b\d{10,12}\b', '[PHONE]', text)
    return text[:80]  # Truncate; never log full user queries

logger.info(f"Query: '{redact_pii(msg)}' | has_image={bool(image_file)}")
```

